,"code_owned":false,"detail":"lifecycle.py and start.py both import the underscore-prefixed fix_commits._branch_only_commits. The stacked PR moved merge-commit listing behind a public gitx helper. This helper could be made public the same way.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F003","line":44,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/lifecycle.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"open","suggestion":null,"title":"Private helper _branch_only_commits is imported from another module","unit":"U0002"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The intent says `start` should keep the runner leased when the validation branch's history can't be read. In `_release_idle_runner`, that relies on `UnreadableFixHistory`, raised by `_branch_only_commits`, being caught by the surrounding exception handler. Only the hidden-commit case and the idle case are tested for reusable `--replace`. The rewritten-branch case is tested only for strict `gc`. If the handler stopped catching `UnreadableFixHistory`, `start --replace` would crash or release the runner, and no test would catch it.","fix_commit":"7f80cc409b20dec560bed2f663fd73e979adaa9b","id":"F004","line":41,"path":"tests/test_release_detached_validation_branch.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Add a reusable test that rewrites `ap/<run_id>` so it no longer descends from the reviewed head, detaches at the head, runs `start --replace`, and asserts that `worktree_released` is still False and the branch tip is unchanged.","title":"No test covers reusable start --replace when the branch history is unreadable","unit":"U0011"},{"action":"no_op","code_owned":false,"detail":"When the branch history can't be read, `_branch_only_commits` raises `UnreadableFixHistory`. The broad `except Exception` catches it and logs a `runner_release_failed` event, even though the code never tried to release the runner. The runner still stays leased, which is the intended outcome. The only problem is that the event log reads as a failed release rather than a deliberate keep.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F005","line":155,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/start.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"open","suggestion":"Catch UnreadableFixHistory on its own and return without logging an event, or log a separate event such as `runner_kept`.","title":"Unreadable branch history is recorded as runner_release_failed","unit":"U0007"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The intent says gc retains hidden-commit runs in both `strict` and `reusable` modes, and that `gc --force` still releases them. Both gc tests use the STRICT config, and no test runs `gc --force` on a retained run.","fix_commit":"98c0463b06fb071f75575118e6cfb67f19646136","id":"F006","line":null,"path":"tests/test_release_detached_validation_branch.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Add a reusable-mode gc retention case. Add a `gc --force` case that checks the run is released and its branch deleted.","title":"gc is tested only in strict mode, and gc --force is not tested","unit":"U0011"},{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"`_release_idle_runner` lets the `UnreadableFixHistory` from `_branch_only_commits` (raised when the branch holds a merge or no longer descends from the head) fall through to the broad `except Exception`. That handler appends a `runner_release_failed` event. Keeping the runner leased here is the intended safe outcome, but the event log reports it as a failed release, and commands.md lists the unreadable-history case and the failed-release case as separate outcomes.","fix_commit":"f634baa583e2693a86529fa03f16dafd2ffedb7a","id":"F007","line":155,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/start.py","response_note":"Resolved by the documented contract: other deliberate holds return without an event; runner_release_failed is reserved for a failed release.","severity":"low","stage":"review"